From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 18:22:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(css): a stray brace broke production while 47 guards said
 green
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The build failed on:

    Syntax error: apps/web/app/globals.css Unexpected } (10408:1)

An earlier edit unwrapped a media query — it removed the rule inside and left
the query's own closing brace behind. One character.

WHY NOTHING CAUGHT IT

Every guard in this repository reads globals.css as TEXT. verify-ui greps for
colour tokens, verify-chrome regexes selectors and declarations, verify-tokens
counts primitives. Text with an extra brace in it reads exactly like text
without one. Not one check had ever asked whether the CSS was valid CSS.

The only thing that would have caught it was `next build` — and I had removed
`next build` from the local command two turns earlier, because it kept being
killed for memory on the Codespace. I took out the one check that covered this
and put nothing in its place. That is the actual mistake; the brace was just
the thing that fell through the hole.

scripts/verify-css.mjs

postcss — the same parser Next uses to compile this file, already a dependency —
is asked to parse every stylesheet under apps/web. It is the parser that failed
in production, it runs in about fifty milliseconds, and it needs no memory to
speak of. It runs FIRST in the chain, because a stylesheet that does not parse
makes every later check meaningless.

It also reports brace depth on the way out. "Unexpected }" is what an unclosed
block looks like several hundred lines later, and knowing whether the file ends
open or closed tells you which end to read.

Two negative tests: the exact orphan brace reproduces the production message and
line number, `Unexpected } (line 10408:1)`; an unclosed block reports
`Unclosed block (line 10403:1)`.

If postcss cannot be resolved the guard exits 2 rather than passing — a check
that cannot run has not checked anything.

48 guards green. tsc unchanged.

